model
```java
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.Formatter;

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Please enter the loan amount:");
        int loanAmount = scanner.nextInt();
        System.out.println("Please enter the number of payments:");
        int numPayments = scanner.nextInt();
        int totalPayments = numPayments * loanAmount;
        double interestRate = 0.05;
        double totalInterest = totalPayments * interestRate;
        System.out.printf("Total interest: $%.2f", totalInterest);
        System.out.printf("Total payments: $% of total loan amount", totalPayments);
        System.out.println("Total amount due: $%", totalAmount);
    }
}
```

This code prompts the user to enter the loan amount and the number of payments. It then calculates the total amount of interest and payments. The total amount of interest and payments are displayed on the console.

The code does not include any validation or error handling. For example, if the user does not enter a number for the loan amount or the number of payments, the code will crash. You should add error handling to the code to make it more robust.

